Rule 1 (real input domain avoids NaNs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8) then min(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)) ∧ (if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 3 (out dtype must be able to hold the result to avoid narrowing cast)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 6 then (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8) else if dtype_(v_1) = 7 then (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8) else if dtype_(v_1) = 8 then dtype_(v_2) = 8 else if dtype_(v_1) = 9 then (dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10) else if dtype_(v_1) = 10 then dtype_(v_2) = 10 else (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
